<tr><td colspan=3>Definition 18 defines solid numbers.  For example, if 18 is presented as 3 times 3 times 2, then it is given as a solid number with three sides 3, 3, and 2.  Solid numbers can be represented as a configuration of dots or cubes in three dimensions.
<p>Squares and cubes are are described as certain symmetric plane and solid numbers.  Of course, some numbers, such as 64, can be simultaneously squares and cubes.</td></tr>
